# Which Android emulators THIS machine uses. Copy to devices.local.sh and fill in:
#
#     cp scripts/dev/devices.local.sh.example scripts/dev/devices.local.sh
#
# The filled-in copy is git-ignored, because AVD names are per-machine: nobody else has yours, and a
# name committed here would be wrong for every other developer on the first run.
#
# List what this machine actually has:
#
#     emulator -list-avds
#
# Why this file exists at all: without a named AVD the `android` target photographs *the attached
# device*, which on a developer's own machine is usually their real phone, holding their real mail
# and diary. A capture run installs and drives a build on whatever it resolves, so the default has
# to be a device you chose deliberately rather than whichever one happens to be plugged in. An
# explicit `--serial` still overrides everything here.

# The phone the `android` screenshot set is shot on; Play's phone slot, and the docs set.
# REQUIRED: there is no sensible default, since it is a name only your machine knows.
MAILCAL_AVD_PHONE=

# Play keeps a separate screenshot slot per tablet size. These default to the stock SDK profile
# names (`avdmanager create avd -d small_tablet` / `-d pixel_tablet`), so leave them blank unless
# your AVDs are called something else.
MAILCAL_AVD_TABLET_7=
MAILCAL_AVD_TABLET_10=
